hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1710","Narrated to us Ibrāhīm ibn al-Mustamir al-Baṣrī, narrated to us ʿAbd al-Aʿlā ibn al-Qāsim Abū Bishr, the companion of al-Lu’lu’.\nAnd it was narrated to us Muḥammad ibn Yazīd ibn ʿAbd al-Malik al-Asfāṭī al-Baṣrī, who said: ʿAbd al-Aʿlā ibn al-Qāsim narrated to me, who said: Hammām ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us, from Qatādah, from al-Ḥasan, from Samurah, who said:\n\The Messenger of Allāh (ﷺ) commanded us to give the greeting of peace to our right and that we should return the greeting of peace to one another.\""\n\nMuḥammad ibn Yazīd added: \""And that we should give the greeting of peace to one another.\""\nIbrāhīm added: Hammām said: \""Meaning during the prayer.\""\n\nCHAPTER:"""""
"1711","\nNarrated to us Muhammad ibn Yahya, narrated to us Muhammad ibn ‘Uthman al-Dimashqi, who said: Sa‘id ibn Bashir narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Samurah ibn Jundub (RA), who said: “The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) commanded us to return the greetings of our leaders, to love one another, and for each of us to greet the others.”\n\nAbu Bakr (a narrator in the chain) said: Allah the Most Blessed and Exalted says,\n“When you are greeted with a greeting, greet in return with one better than it or return it [in the same manner].” (Qur’an 4:86)\n\nAnd in the narration of Jabir ibn Samurah (RA), it is stated: “Then he (the Prophet ﷺ) would greet those on his right and those on his left,” indicating that the imam, upon concluding the prayer, greets those on his right and those on his left. Thus, when the imam greets to his right, the follower should return the greeting from the right, and when the imam greets to his left, the follower should return the greeting from the left.\n\nAllah the Almighty and Majestic has commanded the return of the greeting to a Muslim in His saying,\n“When you are greeted with a greeting, greet in return with one better than it or return it [in the same manner].” (Qur’an 4:86)\n\nTherefore, it is obligatory upon the follower to return the greeting of the imam when the imam greets him after the conclusion of the prayer.\n\n"
